<Layout title="Editorial workflow — Chapter Publishing" description="Prepare, revise, review, and release chapters through explicit editorial states."><section class="page-hero shell"><p class="eyebrow">Workflow</p><h1>Editorial state should be visible at a glance.</h1><p>Prepare the chapter, gather review in context, reconcile changes deliberately, and release a revision whose authorship and decisions remain attached.</p></section><section class="section shell"><ol class="timeline"><li><span>01</span><div><h2>Prepare</h2><p>Define the chapter, contributors, intended readers, source material, and editorial goals.</p></div></li><li><span>02</span><div><h2>Draft</h2><p>Work across supported clients without treating one machine or network session as the sole authority.</p></div></li><li><span>03</span><div><h2>Review</h2><p>Keep comments and proposed changes connected to the revision they evaluate.</p></div></li><li><span>04</span><div><h2>Release</h2><p>Move through explicit approval into a durable published artifact with a reviewable trail.</p></div></li></ol></section></Layout>
